statement.p:
The temperature in Nome was -12 \degreeF at noon. It has been rising at a rate of 2 \degreeF per hour all day.  

Write an equation for the temperature, T, after h hours.


Fill in the table and graph your equation. (Negative values of h represent hours before noon.)



                        ~h~
                        -3
                        -2
                        -1
                        0
                        1
                        2
                        3


                        ~T~
                        \hphantom{0000}
                        \hphantom{0000}
                        \hphantom{0000}
                        \hphantom{0000}
                        \hphantom{0000}
                        \hphantom{0000}
                        \hphantom{0000}


Use your graph to answer the following questions:

What was the temperature 8 hours before noon?

When will the temperature reach -12 \degreeF?

